        },
        {
          "line": 51,
          "text": "Let $S_1,S_2,\\ldots$ be IID with probability vector $P_S$ on a finite nonempty alphabet $\\mathcal S$. Let $\\widehat{\\mathcal S}$ be finite nonempty, let $d:\\mathcal S\\times\\widehat{\\mathcal S}\\to[0,d_{\\max}]$ be finite-valued distortion, and let $D_{\\min}:=\\sum_sP_S(s)\\min_{\\hat s}d(s,\\hat s)$. For $D\\ge D_{\\min}$, let $R(D)$ be the finite-alphabet information rate-distortion function in bits from [[def-it-information-rate-distortion-function]] and put $r(D):=(\\ln2)R(D)$ nats per source symbol. Let $W$ be a finite DMC with capacity $C(W)$ nats per channel use, and fix positive integers $n_k$ with $n_k/k\\to\\rho\\in(0,\\infty)$. For either criterion separately\u2014expected distortion $\\limsup_k\\mathbb E d_k\\le D$, or positive-slack excess distortion $\\Pr[d_k>D+\\varepsilon]\\to0$ for every $\\varepsilon>0$\u2014the following hold for deterministic joint codes as in [[def-it-point-to-point-joint-source-channel-code]]:"
        },
        {
          "line": 69,
          "text": "[F4] [[lem-it-finite-iid-rate-distortion-mutual-information-bound]]: for any reconstruction of $S^k$ with expected distortion $D_k$, $r(D_k)\\le k^{-1}I(S^k;\\widehat S^k)$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
